  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1030 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nQuiet but chilly start to the week expected as high pressure \nbuilds in overhead by Tuesday with 1000-500mb thicknesses of \n524-536dam. This should lead to the coldest overnight temps \nsince last winter/spring with widespread lows dipping into the \nteens with low 20s closer to the lake. The overhead high will \ngradually nudge east through midweek with temps gradually \nwarming back up a bit. Late Wednesday into Thanksgiving \nuncertainty really balloons as the high pressure nudges out. \n\nThe uncertainty with this next potential event on Thanksgiving \nappears to be primarily driven by the development and track of \nthe upper level trough/closed low in addition to its interaction\nwith a developing nor'easter system on the eastern seaboard. \nUltimately the upper levels will become the x factor when it \ncomes to how Thanksgiving plays out. However, there will be \nprecip chances with this, perhaps even some accumulating snow. \nThe best chances appear to be closer to the lake as of right now\nwith potential for some lake enhancement. This will be the \nsituation to monitor over the next few days as models dial in on\nhow the upper levels may play out. Otherwise a brief late week \nsystem Friday/Saturday looks possible as well but this looks to \nbe a weak, fast moving clipper with limited moisture, but could \nbring some rain/snow mix if things come together in the moisture\nfield a bit better.\n\nKuroski",
